From: Lars Karlslund <lars@karlslund.dk>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: t14s: disable camss and crypto for interconnect sync

Sleep test build only. The interconnect providers keep the firmware's
boot-time votes until sync_state, which waits for every DT consumer to
bind. On this tree camss fails to probe (csiphy0 sub-device -EINVAL with
the standalone CSI PHY layout) and QCE has no driver, so the votes are
never dropped and DDR/buses stay at boot level through suspend.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e78100-lenovo-thinkpad-t14s.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e78100-lenovo-thinkpad-t14s.dtsi
index 4fa8a05daa85..5a263aaa5f6c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e78100-lenovo-thinkpad-t14s.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e78100-lenovo-thinkpad-t14s.dtsi
@@ -2276,3 +2276,18 @@ map0 {
 
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Sleep test build: let the interconnect providers reach sync_state and drop
+ * the firmware's boot-time votes. They otherwise wait forever for two
+ * consumers that never bind here: camss fails to probe on this tree
+ * (csiphy0 sub-device -EINVAL with the standalone CSI PHY layout) and QCE
+ * has no driver (CRYPTO_DEV_QCE is not built).
+ */
+&camss {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&crypto {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
